<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Papius Mutilus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 80 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Papius Mutilus was a Samnite general and one of the two consuls of the rebel Italian confederation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a> of 91–87 BCE. He led the southern rebel forces, invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a> and taking several towns, but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>. He later supported the Marians in the civil war and killed himself after Sulla's victory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaius-papius-mutilus.jpg" alt="Gaius Papius Mutilus" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Trustees of the British Museum · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C._Papius_Mutilus,_denarius,_90_BC,_Campana_100.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
